+// RewindBox (patch 0042): with the guest's memory in files (vawin.c, s2a_guest_fd() >= 0) a thread of core 3 alone keeps the tier of the other game threads whatever the number of
+//   performance cores. UTILITY is not only efficiency cores and a low priority: the kernel gives it the second I/O tier, and a fault on a page of the guest files is disk I/O issued by
+//   the faulting thread, held back while first-tier I/O goes on (the other game threads' own page-ins, a screen recording being written). Mario Kart World 0400C3F00006E000 (NPDM core
+//   mask 0x3f: core 3 is an ordinary game core) runs one worker of each of its six-thread pools on core 3. IPA 751 on iPhone17,2, 15 November 2026, a screen recording starting: the
